Well I have been playing a LOT! I'm still quite a newbie for some you reading
this group, but I'm learning ...

I think that this new 3.1 is easier at least in the beginning (I don't know
about the end game). In version 3.0 I got smashed all the time, but now it's
easier or then I have become better.

I really enjoy playing my current game. I had magic resistance in the Gnomish
Mines when I found the polymorph trap ...

"They say that there are hackers avoiding possible spoilers..."










I had my pet still alive and the trap couldn't harm me so I managed to turn my
pet into Master lich! God, that was great. My pet wiped out all monster that
did not attack me. Then few levels later I fell through the trapdoor. I went up
as quickly as I could, but my pet was not tame anymore. I tried to throw food
to it: "Master lich get angry!". RUN RUN RUN!!! Being magic resistant and fast
I could stay alive and finish exploring those Gnomish Mines.

Now I'm going down in the main dungeon. I ate tin of leprachaun meat and my
character teleports every now and then. In one shop I picked up a scroll of
identify and then it happened a teleportation. I should have stolen more and 
I will go and get it! Shopkeeper attacked me and took away half of my HP, then
he saw a bright light and a tunnel ... Kops are after me but I think I can
handle them. I have telepathy, so I don't mind flying cream pies and with my
+3 battle-axe and -6 AC I'm going to survive. Saved my game after killing few
Kops. I killed them all with one hit from my axe (gauntlets of power). I'm
looking for the altar now to get a better weapon. Should also find some way to
get confused so that I can rustproof my current one. I remember seeing one
bat there. You get confused if you eat a bat, right? I might be  playing my
best game so far ...

Still one question: How good sacrifice is a Keystone Kop ?

Waiting for my luck to turn,
